/E (into lactic acid through efficient metabolic pathways. These microorganisms can utilize different substrates, including glucose, sucrose, lactose, and carbohydrate-rich agro-industrial residues, thereby expanding possibilities for reducing production costs. In this context, the use of agricultural and industrial waste, such as sugarcane bagasse, fruit peels, and whey, has emerged as a promising strategy, as it combines cost reduction with waste valorization, promoting sustainability and circular economy principles. Furthermore, solid-state fermentation \(SSF\) has been identified as a promising alternative, as it reduces water consumption, minimizes effluent generation, and presents a lower environmental impact when )
